## TL;DR: What Every Emerald Cut Solitaire Buyer Must Know First

An emerald cut diamond solitaire ring is the purest way to wear this shape. The step-cut facets create a hall-of-mirrors reflection that a solitaire setting displays completely. Every other setting style — halo, pavé, bezel, side stones — adds visual noise around a stone that already makes its own statement.

**The 6-Prong Mistake:** Six prongs on an emerald cut require placing prong metal over the long step-cut facets. Those prongs cast shadows that break the hall-of-mirrors effect. Four corner prongs protect the chip-risk zones and leave every facet open.

