## The 1815-Review Standard

The Classic Four Prong Solitaire has 1,815 verified buyer reviews — more than any other emerald cut setting on the market. That number matters more than any product description or professional recommendation. When 1,815 people buy a ring, receive it, and choose to write a review, they are telling you it photographs the way it looks in the product image, it wears comfortably on a real hand, and the quality holds up long enough to earn a positive star rating.

Call this The 1815-Review Standard: at 1,815 verified reviews, a setting has been tested by a scale of buyers that product photography and marketing copy cannot replicate. The setting is proven. When you don't know which solitaire to choose, The 1815-Review Standard tells you: Classic Four Prong, four corner prongs, consistent quality across 1,815 purchases.

The style earns its reviews on its own terms. Straight shank, four corner prongs, clean geometry. Nothing to catch on fabric.

Nothing to clean around. No side stones to worry about matching the center stone. The emerald cut sits elevated enough to catch light from multiple angles, and the solitaire design ensures there is nothing competing with it for attention.

The Classic Four Prong comes in yellow gold at [$870](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=solitaire&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and platinum at [$1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=solitaire&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Both versions carry the same 1,815-review count, meaning buyers in both metals are equally satisfied. The yellow gold version is the lowest-cost entry point with verified proof of quality.

