## 3 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond Solitaire Ring

A 3 carat emerald cut solitaire is a statement ring. The 3ct emerald cut measures roughly 9.5mm × 7mm face-up — visually comparable to a 4ct round in finger coverage. At this size, the solitaire setting is even more important: any added design element competes with a stone that already dominates the hand.

Natural 3ct emerald cuts start at approximately [$20,000](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for accessible grades and go well above [$50,000](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for D-VS1 GIA-certified stones. At these prices, the setting cost — [$925](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=solitaire&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) to [$2,105](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=solitaire&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — is a rounding error. Choose the setting you want, not the cheapest one.

Lab-grown 3ct emerald cuts currently run [approximately $3,000–$6,000](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for IGI-certified stones. A [3ct F-VVS1 lab emerald cut](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in the Knife Edge WG solitaire gives the visual impact of a natural 3ct ring — estimated at over [$30,000](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — for under [$7,000 complete](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=solitaire&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

